# E00 Agents1: parallel, with random pauses, so the two agents interleave differently at each run; only what does not
# depend on the interleaving is compared: the lines of each agent in order, the receptions of each sender in order (the
# mailbox keeps the order of arrival), the counts, and the turn barrier (every line of the setup turn, "s", before the
# receptions of the next turn, "h").
cover all
fact start ^(agent\d) starting$
fact sending ^(agent\d) sending (\d+)$
fact agent ^(agent\d) (starting|sending \d+)$
fact received ^monitor has received \[(agent\d) -> monitor\]: (\d+)$
fact phase ^\w+ ([sh])
same start bag
same sending seq by 0
same agent seq by 0
same received seq by 0
same phase seq
check start count == 2
check sending count == 20
check received count == 20
fact error (Exception|out of range)
optional error
check error count == 0
